I need help with question 18. The options are unclear.

While evaluating an application for security vulnerabilities, a researcher stumbles upon the following code which they confirm gives them a powerful exploit primitive.

  // Image data
  UINT cbImage = (UINT) pFH->wWidth * (UINT) pFH->wHeight * uBytes;

  m_Format = Format;
  m_pData = pbData;
  m_Pitch = (UINT) pFH->wWidth * uBytes;

  m_Width = pFH->wWidth;
  m_Height = pFH->wHeight;

  // Image data is compressed, or does not have origin at top-left
  if(!(m_pData = new BYTE[cbImage]))
  return E_OUTOFMEMORY;

What subsequent step of the exploitation process will the researcher most likely need to focus their attention on next?

A. Heap Grooming
B. Integer Underflow
C. Use After Free
D. None of the above
